  "fields": {
    "title": "Variable Font",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "A variable font describes a special type of font file. This contains multiple fonts and provides the ability to seamlessly change in defined poles of variation. The technology allows to change the dynamic appearance of fonts. Compared to static font files, variable fonts offer several practical and aesthetic advantages. For one, they are supported by all major browsers, but also have a comparatively small download size. The fact that they consist of a single font file makes them simple to use. By dynamically varying the font poles, the concept makes it easier to animate typography.  ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Possibilities",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "There are many different ways to use the benefits of variable fonts. One example could be to integrate a ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "5Kqa2ZyANgkNAtfUxAU1KP",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "hover",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " effect. This changes the style dynamically as the user moves the mouse pointer over the font. Another effect can be created by changing the size of the screen. The variable fonts align themselves space-filling to the size of the screen. This can be used, for example, to avoid unsightly word breaks on mobile devices. ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
